  "description": "WIGNOT crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C192 H198 Cl2 Dy7 N24 O12 1+,6(C19 H16 Mo1 N5 O1 1+),7(Cl1 1-),66(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Mo1 (Mo) has 1 O neighbors; Mo1A? (Mo) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 1.292-3.835 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 29.17-115.12°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Dy7Mo6C306H426Cl9N54O84. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
